{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1528564341,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzA5MDM5ODg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2640","origin":"github"},"title":"Should make_tempfile use realpath?","message":"`datalad.utils.make_tempfile` calls `os.path.realpath` on the generated path:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/973f9f539510314570a2ab5dd17d04cef7945dc4/datalad/utils.py#L1404-L1406\n\nThis means that `datalad.tests.utils.with_tempfile` resolves any symlinks in its returned path.  In contrast, `datalad.tests.utils.with_tree` does **not** resolve symlinks.  This leads to confusing (at least to me) situations like the one in b4b310458 (more [here]), where a test with TMPDIR=\"/var/tmp/sym link\" will pass when `with_tempfile` is used and fail when `with_tree` is used.\n\nSo I wonder if we should drop the `realpath` in `make_tempfile`\n\n  * so that `with_tempfile` behaves the same as `with_tree`\n\n  * to see if using `with_tempfile` is masking any failures in the TMPDIR=\"/var/tmp/sym link\" case.\n\nBut I don't have a good understanding of this issue because a86f5756f specifically added the `realpath` call to deal with test issues.\n\n[here]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/2634#issuecomment-395847882","files":null}]}